# Every path is owned, so a pull request always requests a review from someone.
#
# ⚠️ CODEOWNERS only has teeth behind a branch protection rule with "Require review
# from Code Owners" turned on; on its own it is a request, not a gate.
#
# A handle here that has no write access is silently ignored by GitHub (no error, no
# review request), so check membership before adding one.
#
# @seandean approves every change: the account that writes a pull request (usually
# @distronode-com) can never approve it, so the owner must be a different person.
* @seandean

# Called out separately because a change to either one lands on users rather than on
# the tree: the release workflow is what creates a public GitHub Release, and the
# capability manifest is what the webview is allowed to ask the Rust side to do.
/.github/workflows/ @seandean
/src-tauri/capabilities/ @seandean
